    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d135">

                <pb facs="0124" n="115" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg115"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.1115A/749b: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul General at Genoa</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Balch</hi>)<anchor n="76" xml:id="d135-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-05-28">May 28, 1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>140. You will please make every effort to get aboard the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Manhattan</hi> every single American who can be crowded on the ship in any
                    possible accommodation before the ship leaves that port.</p>
                <p>Thereafter, if there are any bona fide Americans remaining in your jurisdiction
                    you will please direct them to proceed as quickly as possible to Bordeaux.
                    American Consul at Bordeaux will be advised of the probable arrivals of American
                    ships at that port for the exclusive use of American citizens returning to the
                    United States at their own expense.</p>
                <p>Please repeat to Embassy, Rome for its information.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d135-f1" n="76" type="source" xml:id="d135-f1-content">
                <p>The Minister in Switzerland was informed of this instruction by telegram No. 61,
                    May 28, for repetition to Geneva and such other points as might be benefited by
                    the information (340.1115A/749c).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
